gengtype: rename yybegin, which flex 2.6.5 and later define as a macro

Every C scanner generated by flex 2.6.5 or later defines the function-like
macro

    #define yybegin(s) (yy_start) = 1 + 2 * (s)

(src/cpp-flex.skl in flex; flex 2.6.4 only had BEGIN). gengtype has a function
of its own with that name, declared in gengtype.h and defined in
gengtype-lex.l. The macro rewrites both, and the generated gengtype-lex.c no
longer compiles:

    gengtype-lex.c:146:21: error: variable or field 'yy_start' declared void
    ../../gcc/gengtype.h:444:22: error: expected ')' before 'const'

Rename gengtype's function to gengtype_yybegin. The declaration, the
definition and the one call in gengtype-parse.c are its only uses.

Not from upstream: GCC's master branch still has the clash (checked on
2026-11-13). Release tarballs are not affected, because they ship
gengtype-lex.c already generated.

